3. **Sparsity of \( S \)**: Since each \( S_i \) is sparse, there exists a polynomial \( p_i(n) \) bounding the number of strings of length \( n \) in \( S_i \). The combined set \( S \) contains at most \( p_i(n) \) strings for each \( S_i \) of length \( n + \lceil \log_2 k \rceil \) (due to the addition of the index). Thus, the total number of strings in \( S \) of length \( m \) (where \( m = n + \lceil \log_2 k \rceil \)) is bounded by:
